166 0 obj
<</AP<</N 203 0 R >>/DA(/TimesNewRomanPSMT 10.00 Tf 0 g)/F 4/FT/Tx/Ff 8392705/MK<<>>/P 41 0 R /Q 0/Rect[ 38.835 129.555 573.165 627.165]/StructParent 7/Subtype/Widget/T(remarks)/TU(remarks)/Type/Annot/V(I volunteer to fill mobilization NE-__________-__________, First Report Date/Ready Load Date \(RLD\):_____________.\r______ SECTION A: BREAK BETWEEN MOBS\rIn order to receive orders for the above mobilization, I AM REQUIRED to do the following:\r1. Come off active duty pay \(including leave\) by the following date \( 42 days/6 weeks before RLD\): _____________________.\r2. When meeting with PSD during NMPS demobilization out-processing, do the following:\ra. Ensure the date on DD214 \(Block 12. RECORD OF SERVICE b. SEPARATION DATE THIS PERIOD\) is at minimum\r42 days/6 weeks before RLD.\rb. Sell back or roll over any unused regular leave necessary to meet the DD214 Blk 12.b. date. \(See NAVADMIN 163-12.\)\rc. Sell back or forfeit any unused Post Deployment/Mobilization Respite Absence \(PDMRA\) or "respite leave" to meet the\rDD214 Blk 12.b. date. \(See MILPERSMAN 1050-272.\)\r3. Check-in with my NOSC immediately following my demobilization at NMPS, provide copy of this PG13, and ensure they\rupdate my Individual Mobilization Status \(IMS\) code from RD1 to RD2. \(The IMS code will first change from RM1 to\rRD1when the active duty pay account is stopped. This is normally the same date as the DD214, Blk 12.b. date, but may take\rup to 7 days to change to RD1.\)\r**If demobilizing to create a break in service of a minimum of 31 days, I WILL NOT perform any active duty of any type during\rthis break in service, including AT, ADT, or ADSW \(only IDT or IDTT may be performed\).\r______ SECTION B: ADDRESS CHANGE\rIf also changing to a local address to meet per diem restrictions, I AM REQUIRED to do the following:\r1. After the NOSC changes my IMS code to RD2 per paragraph 3 above, ensure they also go into NSIPS and gain me back into\rthe Reserves \(when on a mobilization or other active duty, Reservists have an active duty NSIPS account\).\r2. After being gained back into the Reserves in NSIPS, ensure the NOSC updates my Residence Address \(in NSIPS\) to a local\raddress for the subsequent mobilization as defined by that location's particular local commuting area. \(Often within 50 miles,\rbut see JTR par. U2800-B for more details.\) Follow MILPERSMAN 1000-100.\r\rOLD ADDRESS: _______________________________ NEW ADDRESS: ______________________\r                                             City/State                                                                            City/State\rI WILL utilize a break in service and a Residence Address change to remove my eligibility for TDY entitlements when I am\rmobilizing to the same geographic area of my most recent mobilization.\rI WILL NOT utilize a Residence Address change during a break in service in order to become eligible for TDY entitlements for the\rmobilization for which I am volunteering.\r______ SECTION C: ISP\rI acknowledge that if I am eligible for Involuntary Separation Pay \(ISP\), by taking a 31 day break prior to the new mobilization for\rwhich I am volunteering and by accepting additional active duty orders, I am no longer eligible to receive ISP.\rI understand that if I do not adhere to the above specified actions, especially if those actions impact the above date I come off active\rduty pay, I am subject to cancellation from the mobilization or other action, as required.\r\r                                                                           ________________________________________\r                                                                           Member- Sign & Date\r**To indicate COMMAND APPROVAL of above plan and the estimated 60 day break necessary, CO/XO or mission equivalent\rmust sign in block below as the verifying official. No electronic service record entry is required other than to forward to USFF N1\rAO or CNRFC N35. In the event supported command needs to cancel agreement due to mission change, 90 days notice is required.)/removed true>>
endobj
